# The working tree is LF on every platform. Git for Windows ships with
# `core.autocrlf=true`, which would otherwise rewrite every checked-out line
# ending on that host — and several things here are counted or compared in
# bytes: §16.3's warm-chunk ceiling measures the sources themselves, and §10.3's
# shim rows compare generated text byte for byte. A checkout must not be able to
# change those numbers.
* text=auto eol=lf
